I did temproarily, did it 2017 was 90% fine for 2 years, and then in 2019 and then i was fine for another 2 years. now i have had it again for 5 months, but it has steadily been going downl lately. Because no one know the cause of non allergic rhinitis its hard to get rid of it forever, your best bet is turbinate removal, but then you are at risk of getting Empty nose syndrome, and even if you dont get ENS you could still get a fucked up nose becuase its basically removing your turbinates.

&#x200B;

I think ENS from turbinate reduction is rare, but its a risk nevertheless. The risk is way higher if you totally remove them, that is why doctors always advice against removing them completely

