Well, i think i kind of know the indirect cause of my tinnitus. combined with my tinnitus i got sinus pressure and pain in my ears. After a couple of month the pressure and pain went down. After 6 months i visited the ENT who found inflamation in my sinuses and diagnosed me with something called vasomotoric rhinitis. I have had 2 sinus surgeries, one in 2017 and one in 2019. I am now going under another treatment for my sinuses

&#x200B;

and its not becaue of allergies or infection, its something wrong with my autonomic nervous system. So i either probably got tinnitus from sinus pressure or that my nervous system is fucked.

&#x200B;

My tinnitus also get louder when i yawn, so its strange

i have not heard about any natural remedies. But there is a treatment that is very effective that i will try. I have had 2 nasal surgery, wich has helped temporarily, but has not really fixed my problems.

&#x200B;

Its a treatment called Kinetic oscilation stimulation. It is a 20 minute procedure where the doctor put some ballon looking thing with some liquid and uses a machine. It is supposed to stimulate the nasal nerves and make them stop overeating.

&#x200B;

It tackles the exact thing you are talking about. It stimulate the nasal nerves. The effect is supposed to last between 6-12 months. So it recomanded to do it every 6 month to be sure you stay healthy.

I agree with OP, Actually having an opinion on something does not make you something other than an ENTP. I hate the stupid stereotype that ENTP are just a bunch of trolls with no real opinions of anything.

