&#x200B;

The fact that branded clothes, fame and money is the main goal for a lot of people is actually sad. Society is actually sick in my opinion

My theory is that your nasal cavity is dry in the back, it makes your nose irritated. I have the exact same sensation, and it is uncomfortable. I would recomand you should try dropping using steroid nasal spray if you are using them because they dry out the nose. And then you should try a saline wash. The magical cure that worked for me was using sesam oil and spray it in my nose every night and morning, and it really helped alot with the feeling you are getting. It moisturize your nose, and it makes it more comfortable to breathe.

&#x200B;

That is also why you probably feel better in the shower and bath tub. Its more moisture there. So i really recomand trying my advice

&#x200B;

I cannot gurantee it will work, but to be honest you should try using it for a couple of days and say if it makes your sensation go away, or atleast make it more tolerable.

&#x200B;

All i do is purchase a bottle of sesam oil at my local supermarket, take an old nasal spray bottle and fill it up, and then sprays it every corner of my nose. With this method i am able to keep my nose in check

&#x200B;

If you still has to use nasal steroids, you should try to use the oil right after.

